Every proposed EARS requirement addition or clarification is given below. The first block states the binding EARS refinements that implement GP-1..GP-4 without narrowing any requirement in `openspec/changes/sherlock-vm-consensus-20261107/general-purpose.md`. The second block provides the explicit **OWNER AMENDMENT** options from D3(i)–(iv) in case the owner wishes to adopt any of those clarifications into `general-purpose.md`.

### 1. Non-narrowing EARS additions for `openspec/changes/sherlock-vm-consensus-20261107/specs/sherlock-ivc/spec.md`

```markdown
### Requirement: In-Circuit Genesis Authentication over Committed Memory (D1)
WHEN a universal leaf proof `U` executes with `h_pre == 0`, the `U` relation SHALL open `prog_d = H("SHK:PROG:v1", prog_root, prog_meta_d)` and `input_d = H("SHK:INPUT:v1", input_val_d, fuel, stack_limit)` and constrain the pre-step processor registers and memory roots to equal the canonical initial state `Init(prog_d, input_d)` (`arena_root = EMPTY_ARENA_ROOT`, `arena_len = 0`, `frame_stack_h = 0`, `task_stack_h = 0`, `deps_d = 0`, `step_counter = 0`, `halted_flag = 0`).
WHEN a run segment is sealed into a completed `RunClaim(prog_d, input_d, output_d, deps_d)`, the sealing circuit (`R` or `N`) SHALL constrain `h_lo == 0` and `halted_flag == 1`.

### Requirement: Universal Register-and-Chiplet Leaf over Variable-Depth Committed State (D2, D3-iv)
The universal leaf relation `U` SHALL have a single fixed verifying key `vk_U` independent of program size, step count, value size, call depth, or helper depth, and SHALL execute `1 <= ds <= S` (`S = 16`) VM steps over a fixed-width processor register file connected via permutation/lookup arguments to PROG ROM, Memory/Stack, 128-bit ALU, and Poseidon chiplets over variable-active-depth (`1 <= d <= 64`) Merkle commitments `prog_root` and `arena_root`.

### Requirement: Two-Level Authenticated Foreign Key Registry and Blake2b Adapter (D3-ii, D3-iii, D4)
WHEN a foreign proof is lifted into the recursion graph, an adapter relation `A_c` for the proof's `VerifierClass` (`class_id = H("SHK:CLASS:v1", arch_bytes, k, exact_pi_count, cs_version, transcript_id, srs_id)`) SHALL verify the foreign proof in-circuit (including full `midnight-ledger:proof[v5]` keyed Blake2b-256 transcript parsing, canonical scalar bounds, and G1 curve/subgroup checks for ledger-format Compact proofs) and output `(vk_id, stmt_d, inner_acc_d)`.
THE core foreign-lift relation `F` SHALL verify the `A_c` proof against `adapter_vk_d`, verify a Merkle membership proof of `(vk_id, vk_d, class_id, adapter_vk_d)` in the public `registry_root`, collapse `A_c`'s proof accumulator with `inner_acc_d`, and emit a `SET` node carrying `ForeignClaim(vk_id, stmt_d)`.

### Requirement: Fixed Core Key Set and Binary Polymorphic Node (D3-i, D4)
THE recursive proof system SHALL have a fixed core key set `{vk_U, vk_R, vk_F, vk_N, vk_C, vk_D}` where `vk_N`, `vk_R`, and `vk_F` share a common `ZkStdLibArch` and domain `k = 20`, and each of the two verification slots of `N` SHALL accept a proof under `{vk_N, vk_R, vk_F}` plus inline PCD claim composition (`SEG+SEG`, `SEG->SET`, `SEG+SET`, `SET+SET`).
```

