# tokenoptimizer

Rules that cut tokens, cost and wall time with no quality loss. Each rule names its evidence id in `~/workflowskills/plugins/tokenoptimizer/EVIDENCE.md`. Measured numbers come from the owner's own logs (baseline: `plugins/tokenoptimizer/baseline/2026-11-01/`).

## 1. Delegate only when it pays

A fresh agent pays a fixed prefix before it does any work: Claude subagent 37.8k tokens, Muse 32.2k, Grok 33.3k, Codex 19.9k (E10).

| Situation | Action |
|---|---|
| A handful of tool calls | Do it inline. Never spawn an agent for a one-step question (E10). |
| Follow-up on the same files | Resume or message the existing agent (E11). |
| Needs the parent's context and the parent is under about 50k tokens (Claude) | Fork (E11, threshold estimated). |
| Independent work over many files the parent should not hold | Fresh agent, narrow brief, file hand-back (E20). |
| Several small questions | Batch them into one agent or one conversation (E07, E10). |
| Breadth-first research | Fan out; stagger same-prefix launches (E12, E41). |

## 2. Briefs and hand-backs

- Point at paths; never paste file content into a brief or a bus message (E20).
- Name the output file. The hand-back is at most 5 lines plus the path.
- Name the model and effort the owner chose. Put any run id or date on the last line, not the first (E08).
- Template: `references/brief-template.md`. Platform recipe: `references/<platform>.md`.

## 3. Read less, in the right order

| Question | First source | Never |
|---|---|---|
| Who calls this symbol, what type is this | Language server (`incomingCalls`, `hover`). An empty `findReferences` means unknown, not "no callers" (E45, E46) | graphify as a caller finder (E47) |
| How is this organised, what touches this area | `graphify query --budget 1500`, then a 40-line window at each location used (E13) | reading `graph.json` or `GRAPH_REPORT.md` whole |
| Literal text, config keys, log lines | `rg`, then a windowed read (E21) | whole-file reads of large files |
| Design rulings, why something exists | `rg -i TERM wiki/index.md`, then 1 to 3 matched pages (E14) | reading the wiki index top to bottom |

Details and failure cases: `references/routing.md`.

## 4. Fetch pages lean

`scrapling extract get URL OUT.md --ai-targeted`, then `python3 scripts/navstrip.py OUT.md` (in this skill's folder) to drop navigation above the first H1. State the size of what you read. Screenshot tiles only when the fact is in the layout (E17, E18, E19). Details: `references/fetch.md`.

## 5. Compact test and build output

- Python fix loop: `pytest -x -q --tb=short --no-header -p no:warnings`. `-x` hides other root causes, so run the full suite before you report done (E50).
- Rust: `cargo check --message-format short`. Write long logs to a file and read the failing lines (E21, E50).

## 6. Keep the cache warm

- One model, one effort and one tool list per session. Do not switch models mid-session through a skill's `model` field (E06, E08).
- agy: put related checks in one conversation, not one `agy -p` each (E07).
- Codex: resume related follow-ups by session id (E09).
- Claude subagent 1 hour cache TTL: see `references/claude.md` (E04, owner applies).

## 7. Rate limits

On a 429, quota or limit error: wait for the reset and resume the same model. Never switch to another model. Model routing by task type is only ever a proposal to the owner (E34).

## 8. Check token use

Run `python3 scripts/audit.py [--days N] [--platform P]` from this skill's folder (in Claude Code: `/tokenoptimizer:audit`). It reads local usage records only, makes no edits and no model calls. The meter itself is `~/workflowskills/tools/tokmeter/tokmeter.py`.

