name: rust-dev
description: Use when reading, changing, building, testing or reviewing Rust code (.rs files, Cargo.toml, cargo, clippy, rustfmt, nextest, rust-analyzer), including the Fenrir sequencer spike and the Moriarty repos. Gives the token-cheap order of work (symbols and compact diagnostics before whole files and raw build logs), the cargo flags that keep output small, and the target-dir and lock-file rules that stop agents from filling the disk or rewriting Cargo.lock.
