    51	| GP-001 | U | GP-1 universal VM. One fixed key set SHALL prove the execution of every program of the Sherlock language, on every input, for every run length below 2^64 and every outcome (`Halted(v)` for every value type, as a digest of a canonical value encoding; `Rejected(code)`; `Exhausted(kind)`); the public statement SHALL carry `prog_d` and `input_d` as data, not circuit constants; capacity SHALL NOT depend on the key (state larger than one leaf's carriers runs against committed memory); a new program SHALL need no new key, contract or ceremony. | One key set and one deployed verifier contract accept proofs of at least three programs the key set was not built from, including one program larger than one leaf's carriers, one run with input, and one run of each outcome kind (row A33). | `general-purpose.md` GP-1; SRC-017 |
