The source confirms two material issues. The recursive stack uses circuits 7.3.0 and stdlib 2.4.0; cand-0c40 cites several nonexistent 0.8.3 paths. Also, the verifier supports single-phase lookups, but a set-inclusion lookup alone does not prove memory consistency. The chiplet design needs explicit write-once or ordered-memory constraints.

