The authentication choice is clear enough to approve. I prefer a separate chiplet leaf as the starting design, but the bus constraints and cost estimates need work, and the inline-versus-lift comparison remains unmeasured. I’ll also flag the proposed 32- or 64-bit storage ceiling as an amendment: GP-1’s explicit height bound does not by itself authorize an address-space bound.

